[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/rename-anything/banner.jpg[/img]
[h1]Rename Anything[/h1]
[b]Made with AI.[/b] I built this mod with the help of AI tools (Claude Code and Codex), and I say so openly. If you would rather not play mods made with AI, do not download it.

Click the pencil next to a name, type a new one and press Enter. You rename your country, its leader and its parties right in the Politics panel, the same way the game lets you rename divisions, armies and fleets. An overlord renames subjects from Diplomacy, and the leader of a faction can rename the faction.

Built on CAPIE (Cyprian's API Extender).

[b]Pre-release.[/b] Tested in single player on HOI4 1.19.3.0 with development builds.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/rename-anything/h-what-you-can-rename.png[/img]
[h2]What you can rename[/h2]
[list]
[*]Your country: name, adjective and flag. The flag picker has every flag in the game.
[*]Your leader, with the pencil next to the portrait.
[*]Your ruling party (short and full name), and the other party groups through tabs.
[*]Your subjects, with the diplomatic action [i]Rename this country[/i]: name, adjective, leader, ruling party and flag.
[*]Your faction, with [i]Rename faction[/i], if you lead it.
[*]States, cities (victory points), generals, admirals and advisers, in the name editor. None of these need CAPIE.
[/list]
A name can use any letter the game can show, Polish letters included, and has at most 32 characters. Names go into your save. After a rename, the same object can be renamed again in 5 days. [i]Restore name[/i] brings back the game's own name.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/rename-anything/h-game-rules.png[/img]
[h2]Game rules[/h2]
In the lobby you choose who may rename (own country and subjects, own country only, or the host renames everyone), whether every country gets a news event when a name changes (off by default), and which flags the picker offers. The host can also switch each kind of rename off for a game. Those switches are new and have not been checked in the game yet.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/rename-anything/h-requirements.png[/img]
[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Hearts of Iron IV 1.19.3.0 on Windows.
[*]Country, subject, faction and flag names and the text fields in the panels need CAPIE: a small native library with its own launcher, plus the [i]CAPIE[/i] switch mod from the Workshop in the same playset.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/rename-anything/h-installing.png[/img]
[h2]Installing CAPIE[/h2]
CAPIE installs with a small setup tool. Close Steam, or let the tool close it for you, and pick one of two ways:
[list]
[*][b]One PowerShell line.[/b] Open PowerShell and paste:
[code]irm https://github.com/capie-mods/capie/releases/latest/download/install.ps1 | iex[/code]
A menu opens: choose [i]Install or update[/i].
[*][b]Download from GitHub.[/b] Get the ZIP, install.ps1 and the two release-manifest files from [url=https://github.com/capie-mods/capie/releases/latest]the latest release[/url] into one folder, then in PowerShell in that folder run:
[code].\install.ps1 -Install -PackagePath .\CAPIE-1.5.0-win64.zip[/code]
[/list]
Both ways check the signed release manifest and every file's SHA-256, install into your user folder (never the game folder) and add the CAPIE launcher to the HOI4 launch options in Steam. The same tool updates, installs an older version, switches CAPIE off or uninstalls it.

Once CAPIE is installed, start the game through the CAPIE launcher. It goes through the Paradox Launcher, so your playsets stay as they are. To play without CAPIE, disable the [i]CAPIE[/i] mod in the playset.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/rename-anything/h-limits.png[/img]
[h2]Limits[/h2]
[list]
[*]Multiplayer has not been tested with two players. Do not rely on it.
[*]No achievements: the mod changes files under common/, which changes the game's checksum. Ironman was not tested.
[*]CAPIE loads only on the exact game build it was checked against. After a game update the game starts without it. States, cities and characters keep working, and custom country names show the game's name until CAPIE is updated.
[*]Esc closes the Politics panel together with an open editor, but the edit mode stays on.
[*]Do not keep a local copy of this mod with the same name next to the subscription. The game then skips the Workshop version. The Paradox Launcher takes the name from descriptor.mod inside the local mod's folder, so rename it there, or remove the local copy.
[*]Mods that replace countrypoliticsview.gui or the same scripted GUIs can conflict. Mods that change states, provinces or victory points need the city tables regenerated.
[*]Some antivirus programs may warn about CAPIE, because it loads itself into the game process. Every release will be scanned on VirusTotal, with the results linked from the release notes.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/capie-mods/.github/main/workshop/rename-anything/h-removing.png[/img]
[h2]Removing it[/h2]
Disable the mod in your playset. Names you set stay in the saves you made. To drop a custom country name, use [i]Restore name[/i] before you remove the mod. Continuing an old save without the mod was not tested, so try it on a copy.

